      <h3 id="by-inches" class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold">Round the finger, in inches</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[62ch] text-text-muted">
        For a soft tape measure read in tenths of an inch. A tenth of an inch round the finger is
        {' '}{(MM_PER_INCH / 10).toFixed(2)}&nbsp;mm, and a whole US size is
        {' '}{(Math.PI * US_STEP_MM).toFixed(2)}&nbsp;mm of circumference — so each row here is about a
        size apart. If your tape has millimetres on the other side, use those and the table above.
      </p>

      <div class="table-scroll mt-5">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[34rem] text-left text-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">
            Ring size from finger circumference in inches, {plain(INCH_LOOKUP_ROWS[0].inch)} to
            {' '}{plain(INCH_LOOKUP_ROWS[INCH_LOOKUP_ROWS.length - 1].inch)} inches, with millimetres and
            the nearest US, UK, EU and Japanese size.
