      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-sm text-text-faint">
        Each row is exact for the figure in its first column; your reading has an error of its own.
        Misjudge a ring&rsquo;s inside diameter by a quarter of a millimetre and the answer moves by
        more than a US quarter size, which is only {usQuarterMm.toFixed(4)}&nbsp;mm. Measure twice.
        If you fall between two rows, type the exact figure into the{' '}
        <a href="/#tool-heading" class="text-accent-text underline underline-offset-2">ring sizer</a>.
        The tables stop at US&nbsp;{rows[0].us} and US&nbsp;{rows[rows.length - 1].us}, the range the
        chart above covers.
